black widow should have been well into  our rear view by now alongside  several other mcu phase 4 flicks but the  covet 19 pandemic delayed the film  leaving us with a big screen drought  but now the movie's new release date is  finally fast approaching  here's everything we know about black  widows so far  black widow had an original premiere  date of may 1 2020 but it was pushed  back  three times as theaters remained closed  across the globe  the scarlett johansson lead flick was  moved to november 9  2020 then again to may 7th of this year  fans were further disappointed when it  was announced this march that black  widow would be delayed one more time  this time to july 9th the movie isn't  expected to shift again as things are  finally looking up regarding the ongoing  global health crisis  most theaters in the united states have  reopened and mass mandates are being  lifted as millions of americans are  getting vaccinated for those still  feeling  unsafe about heading back out to the  movies black widow will also be  available to stream on disney plus the  same day that it's in theaters  subscribers to the platform will have to  shell out extra cash  to watch the movie as it will only be  accessible via premiere access for 29.99  black widow is a prequel story for  natasha romanov taking place between the  events of captain america civil war and  avengers infinity war  we know that some of team cap are on the  run from the united states government at  this point in time after steve rogers  broke his pals out of the raft prison  while natasha was famously on team iron  man she eventually found herself in the  middle  as she aided stephen bucky in their  escape from the airport battle in  germany  unfortunately for her black panther told  secretary of state thaddeus thunderbolt  ross about what natasha did  forcing her to leave the avengers and go  on the run then in avengers infinity war  we learned that she eventually linked up  with steve  and sam wilson and the trio helped  rescue wanda maximoff and vision at the  train station in scotland  as for the 2021 film black widow is  expected to explore the missing  chunk of natasha's life between these  two films which eventually sees her join  up with steve and sam  natasha romanov will link up with some  of the most important people from her  past in black widow this will include  her surrogate family members yelena  bulova played by florence pugh  molina vostikov played by rachel weiss  and alexis shostakov aka red guardian  played by david harper from stranger  things  from the trailers it looks like elena is  going to be the biggest supporting  character of the bunch serving as  natasha's  sister who was also trained in the red  room elena is a spy just like her sister  and she's also gone by the black widow  moniker in the modern era of marvel  comics  many are suspecting pew's character will  become a bigger presence in the mcu  after black widow given her character's  rich history in the comics and due to  the fact that she's set to appear in the  upcoming hawkeye series on disney plus  according to the direct melina and alexi  are mother and father figures to the  girls but they aren't their biological  parents both are also  highly trained and skilled in combat  which was apparent in the trailers  despite alexi putting on a little bit of  weight since his glory days  but as for what we know about their  comic book origins red guardian first  showed up in 1967's avengers number 43  where he was the soviet union's answer  to captain america  weirdly enough he was originally black  widow's love interest although that's  obviously changed for the film  as for vostakov she goes by the name  iron maiden in the comics and she made  her first appearance in 1983's marvel  fanfare number 11  where she was incredibly resentful of  black widow's legend and eventually  became her sworn enemy  there are a few other stars who've  joined black widow in some pretty  noteworthy roles  for example ray winston will portray  drakoff a name  mcu fans might remember from the  avengers when natasha romanov is trying  to lure  information out of loki while he's  imprisoned on the helicarrier  can you wipe out that much red  drakov's daughter the mention of the  name makes natasha go wide-eyed  instantly letting viewers know the  mystery man is bad news from her past  and from the black widow trailers we've  learned dracoff is the superior of  taskmaster and  oversees the notorious red room  additionally ot fegbenlei will be  playing rick mason  someone we assume is pretty important  given he was honored with his own  character poster for the film  rick is one of natasha's only allies and  he apparently has a romantic interest in  her  anything else we can expect from rick in  the movie is a mystery but fagbenly  commented on the character in an  official black widow movie book saying  mason is a finder for people who aren't  so affiliated with armies like people  who are part of the underworld he can  find anything you need as well  he's had a relationship doing that work  for the black widow and they have a bit  of a vibe going on  there's a sense that there's more to  their relationship than it being purely  work related so that's always in the mix  the talent behind the camera on black  widow is just as impressive as the  talent in front of it  the mcu film is directed by kate  shortland who's mostly known for her  films berlin syndrome  lore and somersault black widow is  easily shortland's biggest feature to  date given its 200 million dollar budget  plus jack shaffer and ned benson make up  the writing team of black widow marking  the second official mcu project for  schaefer  the writer famously penned all nine  episodes of wand division which was  praised by critics and fans alike black  widow marks benson's first project with  the mcu  and it's the newest addition to his  rather short hollywood resume  the writer is mostly known as the scribe  and director of the disappearance of  eleanor rigby  while we know the aforementioned dracoff  is going to be playing an important role  in black widow the movie's true villain  is taskmaster somehow after leaks and  multiple release date changes the  identity of taskmaster is still a  mystery but fans definitely have their  theories on the masked baddies real name  who the hell is that guy first appearing  in avengers number 196  taskmaster was a former shield agent  turned assassin whose birth name was  anthony tony masters  taskmaster has the ability to mimic any  opponent's combat skill  which almost always gives him the upper  hand in a fight however  we're not expecting the black widow  taskmaster to be tony masters but rather  someone natasha already knows  this person appears to be some sort of  russian agent who's also in charge of  the red room  and we're suspecting it's someone we've  already seen in the mcu or possibly one  of the newcomers we meet in black widow  is it rachel vice could it be otf  bentley we'll find out soon enough  so taskmaster's whole thing is mimicking  the moves of other superheroes like this  cool spider-man web swing and by  watching the trailers we've discovered  that the big baddie has been doing his  homework in one of the trailers we  watched taskmaster wield a bow and arrow  kind of like a certain avenger we all  know and love  he's even got black panther's claws it  also looks like he's learned a few moves  from captain america with lots of shield  work on display  taskmaster also mimics a famous natasha  move flipping up on one hand and one  knee from a supine position  how he learned her move is a mystery but  natasha definitely has her work cut out  for her if she's essentially fighting  herself  based on the trailers we know thaddeus  thunderbolt ross will be showing up in  black widow william hurt appeared to be  de-aged in his brief trailer appearances  which makes sense given the last time we  saw him was at tony stark's funeral in  avengers end game which was set in 2023  given the timeline of black widow ross  will be around seven years younger  what exactly his role is in the new  movie remains to be seen but he could be  trying to track down natasha after the  events of captain america civil war  tony stark is also expected to make an  appearance in black widow based on a  report from deadline back in 2019  downey's cameo in the movie is expected  to be just that so fans shouldn't expect  much of a storyline from the now  deceased hero  someone else we expect to show up in  black widow is contessa allegra  defontaine  who we met in the falcon in the winter  soldier played by julia louis-dreyfus  according to vanity fair valentino was  first set to appear in black widow but  with premiere dates being pushed back  due to the cobin 19 pandemic things had  to change  whether val will appear is still a  mystery but we know marvel studios does  have big plans for her moving further  into the mcu  with black widow constantly being  delayed over the last year in an effort  to keep fans interested  marvel studios gave us additional  trailers sneak peeks and  featurettes all of these were majorly  dissected as fans did their best to spot  all the easter eggs they could and there  were definitely quite a few moments  people  and objects that stood out in many of  the clips we were shown  some of which might hint at the movie's  biggest reveals one of the cityscape  shots in the trailers was that of  budapest a famous city in mcu lore that  we've never visited before in the  franchise the marvel fandom knows the  hungarian capital well  solely based on comments from natasha  romanov and clint barton in the avengers  and avengers end game we know the  friends have a history in budapest but  just what went down between them or  whatever mission they might have been on  is still a mystery  we also get our very first sneak peek at  little natasha romanov which saw her  alongside a young elena bulova and their  adoptive father alexi  this was well before the girls went to  the red room which we learned about in  avengers age of ultron it looks like we  might see the terrible moment where the  young girls are sent off to be mind  controlled against their will  eagle-eyed fans have also noticed that a  vest yelena belova is wearing in the  trailer is the same one we see natasha  sporting in avengers infinity war  this suggests that black widow could  directly lead into the third avengers  film with not much time in between the  two  when it was announced that black widow  was going to be a prequel some fans were  disappointed since it might not bear any  weight in the mcu  but remember this is the first movie in  phase 4 and you can expect it to  introduce us to new characters who will  stick around moving forward we are fully  expecting elena bulova to be natasha  romanov's replacement in the mcu much  like we saw anthony mackie become the  new captain america in the falcon and  the winter soldier  we're also expecting a little more  backstory on clint barton  but still aren't sure about a possible  cameo taking us to budapest is almost a  confirmation that hawkeye will at least  be mentioned in the movie especially if  taskmaster has memorized his fighting  style  this is all a great tease as to what  we'll also see in the disney plus  hawkeye series and while just a rumor at  this point black widow could also very  well set up the thunderbolts in the mcu  both baron zemo and thaddeus ross have  ties to the group of reformed  super criminals which is currently led  by taskmaster in the comics  black widow is going to be so much more  than a prequel and fans of the marvel  cinematic universe should be extremely  excited for the film we've waited far  too long to see check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about the marvel cinematic  universe are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so 